        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "components list does not include C3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Missing local decoupling on VCC, potentially increasing noise on the supply rail and affecting MCU, display, or NFC stability.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["R11"],
      "pins": ["R11.1", "R11.2"],
      "nets": ["VCC", "GND"],
      "observed": "R11 is a 10 kΩ resistor connected between VCC (pin 1) and GND (pin 2). It is not listed in the specification's component table.",
      "expected": "The specification does not include R11; no bleeder or load resistor is described across VCC–GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R11\") (value \"10k\") (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0603_1608Metric\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"VCC\") ... (node (ref \"R11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"4\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"R11\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Adds a constant 0.33 mA load from VCC to GND, increasing power consumption and potentially affecting battery life or supply margin.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.1"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "U2 pin 1 (VBAT) is on an unconnected net with no other nodes.",
      "expected": "With no backup battery in the design, the STM32L476 VBAT pin should be tied to VCC (VDD) per standard practice and the MCU datasheet.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"65\") (name \"unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1)\") ... (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "no battery, regulator, or USB part appears anywhere in the three .kicad_sch files or PCB.net/PCB.cir"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Backup domain is unpowered; RTC/backup registers may not function, and a floating VBAT can increase current consumption or cause unreliable operation.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain several anomalies: C3 is missing from the netlist despite being specified as a 100 nF VCC–GND bypass, R11 is an extra 10 kΩ resistor across VCC–GND, and U2's VBAT pin is left unconnected instead of being tied to VCC."
}

